{"name":"Nutter Butter","hex":"#f7d4c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nutter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who gathers nuts.","An eccentric, insane, crazy or reckless person."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["nut butter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutter"},{"term":"butter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, fatty foodstuff made by churning the cream of milk (generally cow's milk).","Any of various foodstuffs made from other foods or oils, similar in consistency to, eaten like or intended as a substitute for butter (preceded by the name of the food used to make it)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spread butter on.","To move one's weight backwards or forwards onto the tips or tails of one's skis or snowboard so only the tip or tail is in contact with the snow. Similar to applying butter to bread with the end of a knife.\nTo spin on skis or a snowboard using only the tips or tails being in contact with the snow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nutter Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Nutter Butter is an American sandwich cookie brand, first introduced in 1969 and currently owned by Nabisco, which is a subsidiary of Mondelez International. The manufacturer claims it to be the best-selling American peanut butter sandwich cookie, with around a billion estimated to be eaten every year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Nutterbutter_brand_logo.png/330px-Nutterbutter_brand_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutter_Butter","wikidata":"Q7070573"},{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter","wikidata":"Q34172"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Nutter_Butter_cookies.JPG/500px-Nutter_Butter_cookies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Nutter_Butter_cookies.JPG/1280px-Nutter_Butter_cookies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Nutter_Butter_cookies.JPG/500px-Nutter_Butter_cookies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANutter_Butter_cookies.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/1280px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butter spread on a crumpet using a butter knife","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButtered_crumpet3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/500px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedi